  "problem": "Current-generation retrieval evaluation could overwrite the historical 143-record v1.0.1 baseline. Mismatched cohorts or generations could be compared as improvements. Known absent sources could vanish from the full-universe denominator. Held-out reviewer labels could leak into producer scoring. R07 could be summarized as passing despite failing domains. Editing fingerprint-sealed question-parser.mjs, retrieval-core-v1.2.mjs or controlled-vocabulary.json would break retrieval algorithm fingerprints.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Current-generation evaluation lives in scripts/research-program/evaluate-retrieval.mjs with identities and public questions under evaluation/research-program/retrieval-eval/. The historical 143-record v1.0.1 baseline remains separate; historical EVALUATION.md metrics are not overwritten. Comparisons reject mismatched cohorts or generations. Known absent named sources remain in the full-universe denominator and reduce coverage. Producer tests and independent reviewer labels are reported separately; held-out labels are unused in producer scoring. R07 remains incomplete: failing domains have bounded remediation tasks instead of a passing summary. Fingerprint-sealed question-parser.mjs (10068 bytes), retrieval-core-v1.2.mjs (48161 bytes) and controlled-vocabulary.json (11268 bytes) are unchanged.",
